# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon.
#
# MEASURED IN WEEK 11 and back-ported. This is the reason the file exists.
# Without it the build context of this lab directory is **783 MB**, of which
# **780 MB is `.venv/`** — a virtualenv full of Linux-incompatible macOS wheels
# that the image would never use, because the Dockerfile runs its own
# `uv sync --locked` inside the container.
#
# `docker build` tars the ENTIRE context and uploads it to the daemon before the
# first instruction runs. With BuildKit that transfer is incremental, cached and
# parallel, so the cost is hidden; with the legacy builder (`DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0`)
# it is a single serial tar with no progress output until it finishes — and on
# this context it ran for **26 minutes** having printed nothing but the
# deprecation banner.
#
# The lesson is not "use BuildKit". It is that **a build context is exactly what
# you put in it**, which is the same sentence Week 9 wrote when `README.md` was
# missing from it — the error just arrives at the other end of the range this
# time. BuildKit did not fix the defect; it hid it.
#
# Verify with:  du -sh .    then    docker build --progress=plain . 2>&1 | head -3

# The virtualenv. 780 MB, host-specific, and rebuilt inside the image anyway.
.venv/

# DVC's local cache and machine-local state. Data, not source.
.dvc/cache/
.dvc/tmp/
.dvc/config.local

# Tool caches.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets and local state. `.env` must never reach an image layer.
.env

# Written exercise answers. Committed to git (it is part of the submission),
# but a serving image has no use for it.
answers.md

# Build outputs and vendored installers from earlier weeks.
.kserve/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# The model store (Week 10). The image bakes models/model.pkl and nothing else;
# every other version is fetched at runtime.
model-store/
